<%- include('partials/head') %>
<section class="home-hero">
  <div class="reveal reveal-left">
    <h1>Work your way out<br>of the <span class="accent-text">9 to 5.</span></h1>
    <p class="lead" style="margin-left:0">NoBossly is built for people who still have a job and a couple of free hours a night. It turns the way out into ten levels you climb with real proof — first customer, first dollar that didn't come from your employer, first $1k month, the day you hand in your notice. The XP is a game. The exit isn't.</p>
    <div class="cta-row" style="justify-content:flex-start">
      <a class="btn btn-primary btn-lg" href="/signup">Press start — it's free →</a>
      <a class="btn btn-ghost btn-lg" href="/sample-compass">See a real Compass first</a>
    </div>
  </div>
  <img class="hero-img img-fade" src="https://pub-95ede4ca0cce4b26aa322170b1a5b9f1.r2.dev/Site%20Images/light-bulb_p2diod.png" alt="A way out of the day job, lit up">
</section>

<div class="marquee" aria-hidden="true">
  <div class="marquee-track">
    <span>Built for evenings and weekends ✦ Nobody quits on a whim ✦ Your first non-salary dollar = Level 5 ✦ Quests, not busywork ✦ Ten levels between here and your notice ✦ Daily streaks ✦ A $1k month at Level 8 ✦ Cohort challenges ✦ Get out on a plan ✦&nbsp;</span><span>Built for evenings and weekends ✦ Nobody quits on a whim ✦ Your first non-salary dollar = Level 5 ✦ Quests, not busywork ✦ Ten levels between here and your notice ✦ Daily streaks ✦ A $1k month at Level 8 ✦ Cohort challenges ✦ Get out on a plan ✦&nbsp;</span>
  </div>
</div>

<%# Guarded: the homepage is the last page that should 500 because a route
    forgot a local. Missing paths means the section is skipped, not a blank page. %>
<% if (typeof paths !== 'undefined' && paths && paths.length) { %>
<section class="reveal reveal-up" id="paths">
  <div class="page-head">
    <div>
      <h2>Pick the way out that fits your life</h2>
      <p class="muted">A plumber and a podcaster do not need the same advice, so they do not get the same questions. Your path changes what you are asked, the fit test your idea is held to, and the quests you get.</p>
    </div>
    <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/paths">Compare all paths →</a>
  </div>
  <div class="home-paths">
    <% paths.forEach(function (p) { %>
      <a class="home-path" href="/paths/<%= p.slug %>">
        <span class="hp-emoji"><%= p.emoji %></span>
        <strong><%= p.label %></strong>
      </a>
    <% }) %>
  </div>
  <p class="muted small" style="margin-top:.7rem">The ten-level ladder is the same for everyone. A first sale is a first sale.</p>
</section>
<% } %>

<style>
  .home-paths { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(10rem, 1fr)); gap: .6rem; margin-top: 1rem; }
  .home-path {
    display: flex; align-items: center; gap: .6rem; text-decoration: none; color: var(--text);
    background: var(--panel-2); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 12px; padding: .8rem .9rem;
  }
  .home-path:hover { border-color: var(--accent); }
  .hp-emoji { font-size: 1.35rem; line-height: 1; flex: none; }
  .home-path strong { font-size: .95rem; line-height: 1.2; }
</style>

<section class="stats-band reveal reveal-up">
  <div class="card stat">
    <div class="stat-circle" data-pct="55">
      <svg width="130" height="130"><circle class="ring-bg" cx="65" cy="65" r="54"></circle><circle class="ring" cx="65" cy="65" r="54"></circle></svg>
      <span class="pct">0%</span>
    </div>
    <p class="muted">of American adults have thought about starting a business</p>
  </div>
  <div class="card stat">
    <div class="stat-circle" data-pct="15">
      <svg width="130" height="130"><circle class="ring-bg" cx="65" cy="65" r="54"></circle><circle class="ring" cx="65" cy="65" r="54"></circle></svg>
      <span class="pct">0%</span>
    </div>
    <p class="muted">have taken a concrete step — like writing a plan or registering a company</p>
  </div>
  <div class="card stat">
    <div class="stat-circle" data-pct="37">
      <svg width="130" height="130"><circle class="ring-bg" cx="65" cy="65" r="54"></circle><circle class="ring" cx="65" cy="65" r="54"></circle></svg>
      <span class="pct">0%</span>
    </div>
    <p class="muted">of the people who want to do it have gone past basic research this year</p>
  </div>
  <p class="stats-kicker muted small">Almost everyone stays in the first circle until they retire. The gap is not desire. It's that nobody hands you the next step on a Tuesday night.</p>
</section>

<section class="feature-row single reveal reveal-right">
  <div>
    <h2>🌙 Built for the hours you have left</h2>
    <p class="muted">Most business advice is written as though you already quit. This one starts from the opposite assumption: you have a job, a commute, and maybe ten hours a week that are genuinely yours. Every plan NoBossly builds is sized to those hours and that budget, and anything that only works if you go full-time tomorrow gets flagged before you sink a year into it.</p>
    <ul class="feature-list">
      <li>Your real hours, your real runway — asked up front, then held to</li>
      <li>Quests you can finish on a weeknight, not a 60-hour sprint</li>
      <li>A streak that survives one busy Tuesday — one freeze a month</li>
      <li>Nothing here needs you to quit first. That's the last step, not the first</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="feature-row single reveal reveal-left">
  <div>
    <h2>🧭 Roll your character: your Compass</h2>
    <p class="muted">Every game starts with a character sheet. Ours is drawn from you — a short questionnaire becomes your archetype, your loadout of strengths and unfair advantages, the territories where you have a real edge, and a 5-point fit test built from your own constraints. Then the twist: <strong>you</strong> choose the idea. Your AI advisor stress-tests it against your own fit test and the live market — where it holds, where it strains, and the sharper wedge — but the call is always yours.</p>
    <ul class="feature-list">
      <li>Your archetype, loadout &amp; binding constraints — read back honestly</li>
      <li>Territories worth exploring, with live market temperature</li>
      <li>An avoid list: what's tempting but wrong for your situation</li>
      <li>Draft YOUR idea — the advisor sharpens it, you decide</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="feature-row reveal reveal-left">
  <div>
    <h2>🎮 Ten levels between here and your notice</h2>
    <p class="muted">XP and daily streaks pace you, but no rung can be bought with points — every level gates on something that happened in the real world. AI-planned 7-day sprints and daily check-ins move you rung to rung, and your wins post to a public wall with witnesses.</p>
    <ul class="feature-list">
      <li>🔍 Level 2 — idea validated, 3 real humans gave feedback</li>
      <li>🔨 Level 3 — you shipped something into the world</li>
      <li>⚙️ Level 5 — <strong>your first dollar that didn't come from a paycheck</strong></li>
      <li>🎯 Level 8 — a $1k month: the first month it looks like income, not a hobby</li>
      <li>💎 Level 9 — the one nobody forgets: <strong>you go full-time</strong></li>
      <li>👑 Level 10 — sustained revenue, and your playbook published for the people still stuck at Level 1</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
  <img class="img-corner-fade" src="https://pub-95ede4ca0cce4b26aa322170b1a5b9f1.r2.dev/Site%20Images/light-bulb_2_mns1wm.png" alt="The ten-level ladder out of the day job" loading="lazy">
</section>

<section class="feature-row single reveal reveal-right">
  <div>
    <h2>🌐 Multiplayer, not solo mode</h2>
    <p class="muted">Doing this alone, after work, is how it quietly stops. Cohort challenges start everyone on the same day with one deadline and one leaderboard, the community gives you feedback between rungs, and the Wins wall keeps score in public — first dollars, first customers, resignation letters.</p>
    <ul class="feature-list">
      <li>🚩 Cohort challenges — one start date, one deadline, one leaderboard</li>
      <li>🏆 The Wins wall — real achievements from real members, witnessed</li>
      <li>Daily streaks with a monthly freeze — one busy Tuesday won't reset you</li>
      <li>Everyone here is fitting this around something else. Nobody is pretending otherwise</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="feature-row single reveal reveal-left">
  <div>
    <h2>📚 The library, free and open</h2>
    <p class="muted">Over a hundred practical guides — registering the business, pricing your first offer, finding customers where you actually live, what to do about tax while you're still employed — free to read, no account needed. Start there while you decide whether the game is for you.</p>
    <div class="cta-row" style="justify-content:flex-start;margin-top:.9rem">
      <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/guides">Browse the guides</a>
      <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/locations">Guides by location</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="cta-band reveal reveal-up">
  <h2>Your boss isn't going to fire themselves.</h2>
  <p class="muted">Join free, answer seven questions, and start the climb tonight. Level 5 is a stranger paying you money that has nothing to do with your job — and it's closer than you think.</p>
  <a class="btn btn-primary btn-lg" style="margin-top:1.1rem;display:inline-block" href="/signup">Draw my Compass →</a>
</section>
<script src="/js/home.js?v=5"></script>
<%- include('partials/foot') %>
